# Changelog Conventions

**Always update the Changelog by creating a new markdown file under `Changelog/Unreleased` whose name starts with the current iso date time. Each Changelog update should go into a separate file to avoid merge conflicts, do not edit existing files, reference earlier files from later ones and state what changed/is outdated in the new file instead of updating the old file.**

This project follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) format and adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## Sections and Structure

### Unreleased Folder

- All unreleased changes go into an "unreleased" subfolder of the "Changelog" folder and are moved into the appropriate release folder upon release
- This is where all unreleased changes should be documented

Example structure of a new markdown file `2026-08-18--23-33--changelog-init.md` in the Changelog/Unreleased folder:
```markdown
# Added
- New features

# Changed
- Changes in existing functionality

# Fixed
- Bug fixes
```

### Release Folders

All folders under Changelog except the Unreleased folder should be named like
`X.Y.Z--YYYY-MM-DD`

- Use ISO 8601 date format (YYYY-MM-DD)

## Entry Categories

You may use only these standardized categories as sections (# heading level):

- **Added** - New features
- **Changed** - Changes in existing functionality
- **Deprecated** - Soon-to-be removed features
- **Removed** - Now removed features
- **Fixed** - Any bug fixes
- **Security** - In case of vulnerabilities

Note on Semantic Versioning:
- **MAJOR** (X.0.0): Breaking changes (Removed, Changed with breaking behavior)
- **MINOR** (0.X.0): New features (Added, Deprecated)
- **PATCH** (0.0.X): Bug fixes (Fixed, Security)

## Entry Guidelines

- Start each entry with a dash `-`
- Group related changes together using indentation for sub-items
- Use backticks for code references: `` `methodName` ``
- Be specific about what changed
- Include implementation details, down to the crucial code diff blocks. We do not need a full diff, we have git for that, just the crucial changes with a comment why this was changed might be useful here

Examples:
```markdown
# Added
- Support for custom model providers via `@registry.register()` decorator
  - EECC API provider with Claude Sonnet models
  - Configuration via `.env` file

# Changed
- Updated `extract()` function to accept `model_id` parameter
- Improved error messages for failed schema validation

# Fixed
- Fixed memory leak in long document processing
- Corrected EPC URN format validation for SGTIN identifiers
```

## Best Practices

- **Be specific**: Don't just say "fixed bugs", explain what was fixed
- **For API changes**: Document both old and new behavior
- **For breaking changes**: Mark them clearly and explain migration path
- **For deprecations**: Explain what replaces the deprecated feature
- **For security issues**: Mention CVE if applicable
- **Use consistent terminology**: Refer to features by their proper nameshttps://web-onto-dev.prod-k8s.eecc.de
- Renames `Changelog/Unreleased` to `Changelog/X.Y.Z--YYYY-MM-DD`
- Creates a new empty `Changelog/Unreleased` folder
- Bumps `package.json` / `package-lock.json` and creates git tag `vX.Y.Z`

Do not run the script without unreleased changelog files.

A customer facing Changelog.md file is to be generated from the raw data in the changelog folders by carefully reading which changes went into which release and then filtering and summarising a high level Changelog in the https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/ format directed at customers. While our internal small changelog entry files are technical and detailed, the customer facing summary will be condensed, without code/implementation references and focussing on ux (ui) changes and functionality.
